# Invoke as a tool

The executable procedure lives in `scripts/`. `SKILL.md` is its discovery and
code-mode prompt: select the tool, supply typed input, invoke it, and inspect
the result. Do not reinterpret a prose checklist in place of running the tool.

Keep session/repository/workspace records under `.tkstack/`, protected by that
folder's `.gitignore`. The bundled `scripts/tkstack_state.py` computes (`path`)
or initializes (`init`) private state namespaces. Read-only invocations do not
initialize state. Authored deliverables retain their native/requested paths.

```sh
@SETUP@
@INVOKE@
```

Command files in `commands/` define the same typed interface for CLI and OpenAI
tool calls. Read [subcommands and dependencies](subcommands.md), replace the draft
run signature with the real inputs, and compile before invocation. Use the
bundled `python3 scripts/codify.py commands .` to validate/export signatures or
`python3 scripts/codify.py invoke . -- help` for read-only discovery.
Skillify/Codify supply reserved help/version commands. Omit the command for a
deterministically rendered console manual; use `help --format man` for generated
man(1) source and `version` for the declared package version. These commands
work before compilation and never invoke the workflow. Do not reimplement or
replace their names, routes, flags, or builtin signatures.

